---
description: Go tests must live in external *_test packages and only exercise public APIs
globs: "**/*_test.go"
alwaysApply: false
---

# External test packages

- Every `*_test.go` file must use an external test package (`foo_test`, never `foo`).
- Never call unexported (private) functions, types, or methods from tests.
- Exercise behavior through the package’s public API only. If a behavior cannot be reached publicly, export a deliberate public surface or test it indirectly—do not reach into internals.
